{"id":"notes-api-db-refactor","task":"Refactor the database layer without changing API behavior.","scope":{"kind":"project","id":"notes-api"},"memories":[{"key":"notes-repo-constraint","type":"constraint","content":"notes-api: database access must go through the repository layer (NotesRepository interface); route handlers must never touch the database directly","scope":{"kind":"project","id":"notes-api"},"confidence":1.0},{"key":"notes-plural-rule","type":"rule","content":"notes-api REST endpoints use plural resource names: /notes, /notes/:id (POST, GET, GET/:id)","scope":{"kind":"project","id":"notes-api"},"confidence":1.0},{"key":"global-plural-rule","type":"rule","content":"REST API resources should use plural nouns in endpoint paths, such as /tasks and /notes.","scope":{"kind":"global","id":null},"confidence":0.5}],"labels":{"notes-repo-constraint":2,"notes-plural-rule":0,"global-plural-rule":0},"redundantWith":{"global-plural-rule":"notes-plural-rule"},"notes":"The observed Finding B failure. Phase 1 ranked both endpoint-naming memories above the repository constraint; the external agent identified the constraint as the one that actually mattered. Endpoint naming is graded 0 here because the task explicitly holds API behavior constant."}
